<title>GERMANY: Thyssen, Krupp shares dive in pre-bourse.</title>
<headline>Thyssen, Krupp shares dive in pre-bourse.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Thyssen AG and Krupp-Hoesch dived in pre-bourse trading on Tuesday after the two companies announced late on Monday that Krupp was calling off its takeover bid for Thyssen.</p>
<p>Thyssen opened over eight percent lower at 373.20 marks on the IBIS electronic trading system compared to Monday's close of 410.50, while Krupp lost five percent to 320 marks against an earlier close of 337 marks.</p>
<p>The two companies said on Monday after five days of talks they were planning to set up a joint steel venture and explore other areas of cooperation.</p>
</text>
